nd gave her  time and gave her space and i think from  this moment we become a friend  for more than 20 years amnon a  lieutenant colonel with the israeli  homefront command has been helping with  rescue and recovery missions around the  world is it normal that there are people  that you  find that you just connect with like  that i think this is the first time in  my professional life that i'm talking  with the family i never talk to the  family we try to  totally make  like a wall between the rescuer and the  families because you can't concentrate  and be focused on your work  when you have an emotional thing but  make a is different  it's like  family  their bond forever forged in a moment  where few words were exchanged  hours before mika learned her brother  elon was among the dead i remember  saying hi to him and  you gave me a hug  and i i knew  based on that hug that they had found  him  i didn't have proof but i just knew yeah  and then a couple hours later we got the  call  it was the bond that you already had  yeah  the sign was after  over  12 days we couldn't  say they need to be identified by the  police and so i give her a hug but she  realized something mika and amnon have  built upon that bond with regular calls  and a pact to run the new york city  marathon as a tribute to elon the night  that they found dylan i told him elon  was supposed to run with me my family  was all supposed to be there all is a  hard word for me now did you know right  away that you wanted to run with her  when she told me that elon promised her  to run this marathon and i said i will  run with you i don't think i really  think about it  they've been training together mika from  chicago and amnon from israel exchanging  their stats and keeping each other  accountable i feel like  sometimes you know i'm running i see a  leave fall and i think the building fell  and i go back to the point of time where  i'm thinking how did my brother feel  those five seconds when the building was  falling and i know it's not healthy  but being able to talk about this with  unknown and tell him you know i'm not  having a great day right he gets it  and i think he relates it all back to  the running and says you know you're not  a quitter you're strong  so it gives it definitely gives me that  strength what does it mean  to have somebody who also seems to  genuinely love you and care for you  and cared for your brother even though  he never met him i don't think i could  have done it without him  sorry it's okay  it just means the world i feel like i  have someone watching over my shoulder  [Music]  they're both running in honor of mika's  brother elon but for amnon the mission  extends beyond that part of my running  is the honor for the first responder all  over the world we are very similar  we are leave everything we are willing  to suffer we are willing to sacrifice  and we are willing to go and put  ourselves in danger  to help people it's all a journey you  know in the marathon it is a journey  it's not about finishing but it's like  how you get through each mile at a time  right and so i think it was really that  analog of  life is uncertain you don't know what  the next smile might bring  but you got to take it step by step  [Music]  very wise words on marathon day mika  will be wearing shoelaces from a pair of  running shoes that her brother gave her  so that she can keep him close her  fiance made a tag for the sneakers also  which reads what doesn't kill you makes  you stronger and mika and amnon are  going to be wearing matching shirts they  were designed by amnon's daughter  he's the father of five the oldest is  his only daughter and she's around  mika's age and he told me that was just  another part of their bond that this is  it's a family bond it's like a  father-daughter type of bond and a  friendship obviously but you could feel  it through the zoom even though we  obviously didn't have them together in  person because it's today when